  "type": "multipleCorrect",
  "level": 3,
  "question": {
    "text": "<p>One end of a horizontal uniform beam of weight&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>W</mi></math> and length&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>L</mi></math>&nbsp;is hinged on a vertical wall at point&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>O</mi></math> and its other end is supported by a light inextensible rope. The other end of the rope is fixed at point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi></math>, at a height&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>L</mi></math> above the hinge at point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>O</mi></math>. A block of weight&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi><mi>W</mi></math> is attached at the point&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math> of the beam, as shown in the figure (not to scale). The rope can sustain a maximum tension of&nbsp; <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfenced><mi>W</mi></math>. Which of the following statement(s) is(are) correct?</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/7a933026-8e1f-4a4f-99cb-f529a1abd116-image.png\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 240px;\" />&nbsp;</p>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "hfOaE",
      "text": "The vertical component of reaction force at&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>O</mi></math>&nbsp;does not depend on&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi></math>.",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "dgP4y",
      "text": "The horizontal component of reaction force at&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>O</mi></math>&nbsp;is equal to&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>W</mi></math>&nbsp;for&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn></math>.",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "F4rz4",
      "text": "The tension in the rope is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">W</mi></math>&nbsp;for&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn></math>.",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "HyApj",
      "text": "The rope breaks if&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn></math>.",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/a08c0803-1477-434a-87da-a3342ffb71ba-image.png\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 253px;\" />&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8757;</mo></math>&nbsp;Rod is in equilibrium, net torque on the rod about&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>O</mi></math>&nbsp;will be zero.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>W</mi><mfenced><mfrac><mi>l</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mi>&#945;</mi><mi>W</mi><mfenced><mi>l</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>T</mi><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mfrac><mi>l</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mi>&#945;</mi><mi>W</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>T</mi><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mfrac><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mi>W</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced></math></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Now checking options-</p><p>(A)</p><p>Force balance on rod,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>T</mi><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi>W</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>&#945;</mi><mi>W</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>&#945;</mi><mi>W</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>-</mo><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mi>&#945;</mi><mi>W</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>Hence, option (A) is correct.</p><p>(B) Write horizontal force equation,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>T</mi><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mfrac><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>&#8658;</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>W</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>If&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn></math>,&nbsp;then,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>W</mi></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mi>W</mi></math></p><p>Hence, option (B) is correct.</p><p>(D)&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo></math>&nbsp;Maximum Tension of string&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">W</mi></math></p><p>So,&nbsp;to break.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>T</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">W</mi><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>&#8658;</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">W</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#945;</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#62;</mo><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">W</mi><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#945;</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn></math></p><p>So, string will break.</p><p>option (D) correct.</p>",
